-- title:
--   Common domain generating both branch and level-one function fields
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$ and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage` for $p$, i.e. a package of data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full level-$p$ modular curve over $\mathbb Z$ with structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O$ for the base change $\mathrm{DRModel}\,p \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$, let $C = (\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ be the curve over $k$ attached by the package to $k$, with structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and let $\xi$ be the image of the generic point of $C$ under the morphism $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap` $\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Let $\psi$ be a ring homomorphism from the residue field of the local ring of $X_O$ at $\xi$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, the subfield of $k((T))$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`. Assume that for every $a \in O$, $\psi$ sends the residue class of the germ at $\xi$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained from $a$ along the second projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ to the image of $\mathrm{to}\kappa(a)$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, and that $\psi$ takes at least one value outside the image of $k$. Then there exist a commutative domain $D$ and ring homomorphisms $\iota_k : k \to D$, $\iota_\kappa$ from the residue field at $\xi$ to $D$, $\Theta : D \to C.\mathrm{functionField}$ and $\Psi : D \to \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$ such that $\Theta \circ \iota_k$ is the structural embedding `baseToFunctionField` of $k$ into the function field of $C$, $\Theta \circ \iota_\kappa$ is the map induced on residue fields by the stalk map at the generic point of $C$ of the above morphism, $\Psi \circ \iota_k$ is the algebra map $k \to \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, $\Psi \circ \iota_\kappa = \psi$, $\Theta$ is injective, every element of $C.\mathrm{functionField}$ is of the form $\Theta(a)/\Theta(b)$ with $\Theta(b) \neq 0$, and $\Psi$ is injective.
--
--   This is the descent step showing that a place-specialisation map $\psi$ out of the residue field of the component $\mathrm{comp}_0$ of the Deligne–Rapoport fibre in characteristic $p$ is automatically injective once it is non-constant: both the function field of that component and the level-one fibre field are generated from one common domain, whose function field has transcendence degree one over $k$. It is used by the two statements identifying the relevant residue field with a rational function field compatibly with the stalk maps at the generic point.
-- source:
